      "content": "305|characters regain their original hit point maximums, lose their proficiency with Chaos Control, and their physical and mental states revert to normal. The party can force the slaad to perform any other action they desire, so long as they remain in control of its control gem. \n306|\n307|The Zerthimon Steelbeast brings them back to Lez'lin's monastery, where she reunites with Zardan if the party summoned him. They exchange words of mourning over their brother Drarth's passing, and thank the group for risking their lives for this mission. The Githzerai then make plans to inform their people of a Material Plane citadel's fall and the Steelbeast expresses its wish to continue eradicating aberrations with them, despite its attachment to the creature attuned to it. \n308|\n309|Everyone bids each other farewell before the planar hourglass's four hours are up and the party is gently displaced back to the Material Plane. \n310|\n311|## Rewards\n312|\n313|- **1,200 XP each** for completing the adventure. This is a Tier 1 deadly or major adventure; award partial XP for incomplete progress using [[Character Advancement]].\n314|- **300 gp total** from the [[N.E.R.D]] research contract, divided among the characters as the party decides.\n315|- **FLS contract completion** recorded at the [[FLS Guildhall]].\n316|- **N.E.R.D research credit** and a favorable academic reference if the party returns its notes, samples, and an explanation of the breach.\n317|- **Favor with the Zooka Mire Collective** if the party prevents contaminated materials from spreading through [[Zooka Mire]].\n318|- **Faction consequences or favors** based on who receives the recovered Arcanite, Magitech, slaad remains, control gem, and Githzerai equipment.\n319|- **Slaad monster components**, if the party safely harvests them and a faction or the DM permits the harvest.\n320|- The **planar hourglass**, **planar recall bead**, **spell scroll of imprisonment**, and **Zerthimon Steelbeast** are temporary or objective-specific rewards and cannot be kept unless the DM explicitly awards them.\n321|\n322|Record any lasting curses, diseases, faction changes, debts, favors, or story awards as described in [[Character Advancement]].\n323|\n324|## Appendix A: Zardan Character Sheet\n325|\n326|### Zardan\n327|\n328|| Field | Value |\n329||---|---|\n330|| **Class & Level** | Wizard 3 (Divination) |\n331|| **Race** | Githzerai |\n332|| **Background** | Sage |\n333|| **Alignment** | Lawful Neutral |\n334|| **Proficiency Bonus** | +2 |\n335|| **Armor Class** | 12 |",
