      "content": "1|# Adventure Summary\n2|\n3|**Curse of Slaad** is a planar monster hunt beginning at the [[FLS Guildhall]] on [[Nevercough Island]] and leading into [[The Outback]] near [[Zooka Mire]]. A N.E.R.D research outpost has gone silent while monitoring strange magical disturbances connected to the [[Arcanite]] deposits around [[Mount Zooka]]. The party must investigate the missing researchers, determine what entered the outpost, and prevent a dangerous planar threat from spreading into [[Stickyickistan]].\n4|\n5|# The Rolling Papers Advertisement\n6|\n7|**Submitted by:** [[N.E.R.D]] Planar Studies Faculty  \n8|**Tier:** Tier 1  \n9|**Recommended Level:** 3  \n10|**Expected Length:** One-shot, approximately 4–6 hours  \n11|**Tone:** Planar horror, monster hunt, magical investigation, heroic danger  \n12|**Location:** [[Nevercough Island]] / [[The Outback]] / [[Zooka Mire]]\n13|\n14|## Headline\n15|\n16|> **N.E.R.D SEEKS LICENSED ADVENTURERS AFTER PLANAR RESEARCH OUTPOST FALLS SILENT**\n17|\n18|## Public Notice\n19|\n20|The planar-studies faculty of [[N.E.R.D]] is seeking capable adventurers to investigate a failed research outpost near [[Zooka Mire]]. The outpost was established to monitor disturbances in the Weave around the [[Arcanite]]-rich regions near [[Mount Zooka]], but its researchers have stopped responding to messages and magical communication.\n21|\n22|The FLS is authorized to investigate the site, locate any survivors, identify the cause of the disturbance, and prevent further danger to [[Stickyickistan]]. Applicants should be prepared for wilderness travel, hostile creatures, and unstable magic.\n23|\n24|Interested adventurers should register at the [[FLS Guildhall]] on [[Nevercough Island]].\n25|\n26|# The Roach Clip Advertisement\n27|\n28|**Posted by:** An anonymous recovery broker  \n29|**DM:** Chase  \n30|**Tier:** Tier 1  \n31|**Recommended Level:** 3  \n32|**Expected Length:** One-shot, approximately 4–6 hours  \n33|**Tone:** Planar horror, artifact recovery, monster harvesting, faction pressure  \n34|**Location:** [[Zooka Mire]] / Limbo  \n35|**Legality:** Gray, with several interested claimants\n36|\n37|## Coded Notice\n38|\n39|> **The swamp station stopped answering. The frogs inside are not ordinary frogs. Recover the research gear, any useful stones, and anything that can be sold before the official investigators finish their paperwork. Do not bring the infection home. Payment for intact specimens.**\n40|\n41|# What Players Should Know\n42|\n43|- **Content / vibe:** Planar horror, body horror, dangerous magic, academic negligence, and dark comedy.\n44|- **Combat / roleplay / exploration mix:** Investigation, wilderness travel, dungeon exploration, and high-risk combat.\n45|- **Character hooks:** Good for monster hunters, researchers, Free League contractors, bounty hunters, explorers, or adventurers protecting Stickyickistan.\n46|- **Special notes:** Expect unstable magic, strange environments, and limited opportunities to rest. Characters with Arcana, Medicine, Survival, or monster-hunting skills may be especially useful.\n47|- **Faction ties:** Characters may have connections to [[N.E.R.D]], the [[Free League of Stickyickistan]], the [[Ashen Shadow Society]], or other Stickyickistan factions.\n48|- **Lines not to cross:** The adventure includes infection and body horror. Discuss comfort levels before play.\n49|\n50|# Rewards\n51|\n52|- **1,200 XP each** for completing the adventure\n53|- **300 gp total** from the [[N.E.R.D]] planar studies faculty\n54|- N.E.R.D research credit and a favorable academic reference\n55|- Slaad monster components, if safely harvested.\n56|\n57|# Sign-Up\n58|\n59|**DM:** Initiate of Tribulation, Vorg Lordcaster  \n60|**Date / Time:** TBD  \n61|**Seats:** 4–6 players  \n62|**How to join:** Register through the [[FLS Guildhall]] / post in the Free League chat.",
